# The cpu microcode loaded next to the kernel. The kernel itself is NOT here:
# it is the one part of the core that is properly per-distro - a desktop and an
# appliance want different drivers built in, different console behaviour and
# different boot times. Each distro names the kernel package it wants in its own
# packages.list. This list is concatenated with the distro's, so anything left
# here would be installed alongside whatever the distro chose.
12-make-cpio.tar.gz
3-make-microcode.tar.gz
